window.RDG={"img":"","img_index":1,"img_label":"Pullover","lab":{"example":"Every small model here trains on <b>Fashion-MNIST</b>: 70,000 grey 28 &times; 28 images of clothing in 10 classes (MIT licence, Zalando), padded to 32 &times; 32; clothing shows blur, dropped modes and class confusions by eye, and a 1M-parameter U-Net learns it in minutes on a laptop GPU. Sixteen fixed test images are used for every before/after. The pretrained models, pinned to exact revisions, are <b>Stable Diffusion v1.5</b> (CreativeML OpenRAIL-M), <b>CLIP ViT-B/32</b>, <b>SigLIP 2 base</b> and the VLM <b>SmolVLM-500M-Instruct</b> (both Apache 2.0), run on sixteen colour test images with known answers (photographs in the public domain or CC0, synthetic scenes, Stable Diffusion outputs). Details and licences: the root's <code>src/data/README.md</code>.","sd_params":"Counted from the pinned v1.5 weights: U-Net 859,520,964, VAE 83,653,863, text encoder 123,060,480 parameters <span class=\"meas\">measured</span> (setup, <code>src/data/smoke/sd.json</code>), matching the README's 860M and 123M.","sdvae":"On the cat photograph, the v1.5 VAE (fp16) turns 512 &times; 512 &times; 3 into 4 &times; 64 &times; 64 and back at 30.9 dB PSNR; the raw latent's standard deviation is 4.13, and 0.753 after multiplying by 0.18215 <span class=\"meas\">measured</span> (setup smoke test): the factor brings it near, not exactly to, 1. <span data-rd=\"sdvae_more\" class=\"rd-todo\">TODO (Latent lab): all fixed images, and what decoding without the factor does.</span>","sd_time":"One 512 &times; 512 image, 25 DPM-Solver steps with guidance 7.5 (fp16): 21.0 s median, 0.84 s per step with its two batched passes, peak 7.5 GB; with attention slicing 16.9 s and 4.45 GB <span class=\"meas\">measured</span> on Apple M1 Pro (setup smoke tests). A datacenter GPU is many times faster per step; the step count is the same. <span data-rd=\"sd_time_more\" class=\"rd-todo\">TODO (Diffusion lab): the per-pass and per-decode split.</span>","clip":"CLIP ViT-B/32 prefers \"a photo of a cat\" for the cat photograph (cosine 0.2845 against 0.2318 for \"a photo of a dog\") and flips to \"dog\" once a <code>DOG</code> sticker is added (0.2775 against 0.2855); SigLIP 2 does not flip (0.1281 against 0.1112), and SmolVLM still answers \"There is a cat in this image.\" <span class=\"meas\">measured</span> (setup smoke tests). <span data-rd=\"clip_more\" class=\"rd-todo\">TODO (Vision lab): zero-shot accuracy of CLIP and SigLIP 2 on the labelled set.</span>","vlm_tokens":"SmolVLM-500M turns one 512 &times; 512 image into <b>1,088 image tokens</b>: its processor scales the image up to 2,048 pixels on the long side, cuts 4 &times; 4 = 16 tiles of 512 plus one downscaled whole view, and each tile becomes 64 tokens after a pixel shuffle; a one-sentence question then makes a 1,142-token prompt <span class=\"meas\">measured</span> (setup smoke test, <code>vlm.json</code>). Twice LLaVA-1.5's 576 for a smaller model: tiling is what lets small VLMs read detail. <span data-rd=\"vlm_tokens_more\" class=\"rd-todo\">TODO (VLM lab): counts at other resolutions and the full prompt.</span>","fid_n":"On this page's data, real Fashion-MNIST training images scored against the 10,000 real test images (so nothing is wrong) give FID 2.54 at 10,000 images, 3.84 at 5,000, 15.4 to 15.8 at 1,000, 27.9 to 28.1 at 500 and 44.9 to 47.4 at 250 <span class=\"meas\">measured</span> (setup, <code>fid_floor.json</code>, three draws below 10,000)."}};
